<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $118.1 mln May 26.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $118.1 mln May 26.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $118.1 million deficit on May 26 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 26</p>
<p>Exports: $197.1 million</p>
<p>Imports: $225.8 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $211.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $300.8 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $118.1 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UPDATE</p>
<p>Exports: $4.294 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $4.466 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.505 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $4.360 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $973 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
